language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ session3_kidney_exchange: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ At a hospital, n people are on a waiting list for a kidney transplant. Compatibility is a directed graph: compatible[i] is the set of people to whom person i can donate. Anyone who gives a kidney must receive one, and no person receives more than one kidney. Maximise the number of people who receive a new kidney.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `session3_kidney_exchange.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/session3_kidney_exchange.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `session3_kidney_exchange_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py session3_kidney_exchange.json
$   savilerow model.eprime session3_kidney_exchange_1.param -run-solver

$ num_people: the number of people on the waiting list, numbered 1 to num_people
given num_people : int(1..)
$ compatible_dim2: the longest list of people any one person can donate to (derived by the converter from the data)
given compatible_dim2 : int(1..)
$ compatible[i,k]: the k-th person that person i can donate to (1-based; rows shorter than compatible_dim2 are padded with 0, which no person has)
given compatible : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_people), int(1..compatible_dim2)] of int(0..num_people)

$ transplants[i,j]: person i donates a kidney to person j
find transplants : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_people), int(1..num_people)] of bool

$ search hint: branch on the transplants first and use conflict-driven search (speeds up the search)
branching on [transplants]
heuristic conflict

maximising (sum i : int(1..num_people) . sum j : int(1..num_people) . toInt(transplants[i,j]))

such that
$ a donation from i to j is allowed only if j is in the compatibility list of i
forAll i, j : int(1..num_people) . (transplants[i,j] -> (exists k : int(1..compatible_dim2) . compatible[i,k] = j)),
$ no person gives more than one kidney
forAll i : int(1..num_people) . (sum j : int(1..num_people) . toInt(transplants[i,j])) <= 1,
$ no person receives more than one kidney
forAll j : int(1..num_people) . (sum i : int(1..num_people) . toInt(transplants[i,j])) <= 1,
$ anyone who gives a kidney must receive one
forAll i : int(1..num_people) . (sum j : int(1..num_people) . toInt(transplants[i,j])) <= (sum j : int(1..num_people) . toInt(transplants[j,i]))
